# UI diagnostic audit: 2026-11-10

## Target

Barroga frontend-next. Web application using Next.js 16.4.5, React 19, and Tailwind 4.
The user requests a minimal, clean UI and confirms the original dark colors and purple accents.

## Applied changes

- Preserve the original theme colors, logo color, authentication behavior, and staged page copy.
- Simplify the login form and improve spacing and typography.
- Add a compact responsive navigation layout, desktop sidebar, and account header.
- Keep mobile account identity available to screen readers and add a skip link.
- Show total, available, and adopted counts derived from the existing animal response.
- Restyle tables, controls, and status labels consistently.
- Give record search full width on mobile.
- Contain absolute screen-reader table headings inside the table scroll region.
- Preserve the existing sign-out confirmation and all original event handlers.

## Verification

- Production build passes.
- TypeScript noEmit check passes.
- Existing Vitest suite: 14 tests pass across 3 files.
- Browser checks use isolated mocked API responses, with no real accounts or record writes.
- Login, dashboard, animal table, and adopter portal fit widths 320, 375, 425, 768, 1024, 1440.
- Registration, sign-out dialog, and animal editor fit at 320 pixels.
- Check empty login validation, registration toggle, password visibility, navigation, record search,
  sign-out cancellation, derived counts, and mobile account accessibility.
- No browser page errors occur in the smoke pass.
- Lint retains 11 existing errors and 2 existing warnings. Baseline comparison finds no new diagnostics.
- Screenshots remain in .sauron/ui-review/. Backups and checksums use ConflictManager.

## Local preview

http://127.0.0.1:3100

No dependency, backend, authentication, or deployment changes are part of this UI work.

## Login page refinement

- Preserve the original dark background and purple primary color.
- Add a framed welcome panel with a generated decorative dog-and-cat portrait.
- The optimized public/login-companions.webp asset is 1086 by 1448 pixels and 88,346 bytes.
- Add labeled field icons, password visibility icons, and a clearer submit/loading state.
- Simplify the account-mode prompt and keep the mobile header compact.
- Input borders retain the original higher-contrast control color.
- Keep the loading status outside an aria-busy region so it can announce promptly.
- Authentication state and handlers match the pre-edit source exactly.
- Sign-in and registration fit 320, 375, 425, 768, 1024, and 1440 pixel widths.
- Browser checks cover invalid credentials, email format, password mismatch, visibility toggles,
  mode switching, busy feedback, duplicate-submit locking, and successful mocked sign-in.
- Build, typecheck, and all 14 existing tests pass. No new lint diagnostics appear.
- Login screenshots use the login-v2 prefix in .sauron/ui-review/.
